   {:kind :function,
    :name "mino_empty_list",
    :return-type "mino_val *",
    :params "mino_state *S",
    :signature "mino_val *mino_empty_list(mino_state *S);",
    :doc
    "Return the singleton empty-list value `()`. Distinct from nil:\n`seq?` is true, `nil?` is false, `empty?` is true, and `=` against\nnil is false. Walkers using `mino_is_cons` terminate on it because\nthe type tag is MINO_EMPTY_LIST, not MINO_CONS."}
   {:kind :function,
    :name "mino_int",
    :return-type "mino_val *",
    :params "mino_state *S, long long n",
    :signature "mino_val *mino_int(mino_state *S, long long n);",
    :doc
    "Create an integer value from a signed long long. Total over the full\nlong long range. Values in [-2^60, 2^60 - 1] return a tag-encoded\npointer (no allocation). Values outside that band depend on the\nMINO_CAP_BIGNUM capability: with bignum installed, the result is a\nMINO_BIGINT carrying the same numeric value, so hosts that opt in\nto arbitrary-precision arithmetic see one int family that grows\npast 64 bits transparently; without bignum, the result is a boxed\nMINO_INT cell that still holds the full 64-bit signed integer.\n\nInside mino's runtime, deterministic operations such as the reader,\nbitwise primitives, and the unchecked-* family never auto-promote;\nthey keep producing MINO_INT (boxed when outside the tag range) so\nClojure-style \"long stays long\" semantics are preserved.\n\nCapability-conditional behaviour\n--------------------------------\nThe auto-promote of a tag-overflowing `mino_int` argument to a\nMINO_BIGINT when MINO_CAP_BIGNUM is installed is the C-side peer\nto JVM Clojure's `+'` / `inc'` / `*'` / `dec'` opt-in arithmetic.\nAn embedder that wants \"long stays long\" (regardless of magnitude)\nuses `mino_install_minimal` plus the explicit `unchecked-*`\nsurface; an embedder that wants the JVM `BigInteger`-shaped\n\"promote silently\" semantics installs the BIGNUM capability and\ngets the auto-promote through this constructor."}
   {:kind :function,
    :name "mino_float",
    :return-type "mino_val *",
    :params "mino_state *S, double f",
    :signature "mino_val *mino_float(mino_state *S, double f);",
    :doc "Create a floating-point value."}
   {:kind :function,
    :name "mino_float32",
    :return-type "mino_val *",
    :params "mino_state *S, double f",
    :signature "mino_val *mino_float32(mino_state *S, double f);",
    :doc
    "Create a 32-bit single-precision floating-point value. The double\nargument is narrowed to float and stored back as a double so\nequality / print see the rounded value; the type tag distinguishes\nit from `MINO_FLOAT` so `double?` returns false on the result."}
   {:kind :function,
    :name "mino_bigint_from_ll",
    :return-type "mino_val *",
    :params "mino_state *S, long long n",
    :signature
    "mino_val *mino_bigint_from_ll(mino_state *S, long long n);",
    :doc "Create a bigint from a signed long long."}
   {:kind :function,
    :name "mino_bigint_from_string",
