    :doc
    "Create a bigint by parsing a base-10 numeric string (optional leading\n'+' or '-'). Returns NULL on parse failure."}
   {:kind :function,
    :name "mino_ratio_from_ll",
    :return-type "mino_val *",
    :params "mino_state *S, long long num, long long denom",
    :signature
    "mino_val *mino_ratio_from_ll(mino_state *S, long long num, long long denom);",
    :doc
    "Create a rational from numerator and denominator long longs. The result\nis reduced (gcd = 1) and normalised so the denominator is positive.\nIf denom is zero, throws division-by-zero. If the result is integer,\nreturns a MINO_INT or MINO_BIGINT instead of a MINO_RATIO."}
   {:kind :function,
    :name "mino_bigdec_from_string",
