    "C-callable transformer used by mino_tx_alter_c / mino_tx_commute_c.\n`cur` is the in-tx effective value at call time; `user` is the\ncaller-supplied opaque pointer. Returns the new value. May call\nmino_call for nested Clojure dispatch and may throw via\nprim_throw_classified -- both unwind through the enclosing tx\nrunner. The function pointer must remain valid for the lifetime of\nthe transaction (in particular: across retries and through commit-\ntime replay for commute)."}
   {:kind :function,
    :name "mino_tx_alter_c",
    :return-type "mino_val *",
    :params
    "mino_state *S, mino_val *v, mino_tx_xform_fn fn, void *user, mino_env *env",
    :signature
    "mino_val *mino_tx_alter_c(mino_state *S, mino_val *v, mino_tx_xform_fn fn, void *user, mino_env *env);",
    :doc
    "Apply (fn cur user) to ref's current in-tx value and store the\nresult. Records a read for read-set validation. Must be called from\ninside a transaction. Returns the new value, or NULL if the\ntransformer threw. Equivalent to (alter ref #(fn % user))."}
   {:kind :function,
    :name "mino_tx_commute_c",
    :return-type "mino_val *",
    :params
    "mino_state *S, mino_val *v, mino_tx_xform_fn fn, void *user, mino_env *env",
    :signature
    "mino_val *mino_tx_commute_c(mino_state *S, mino_val *v, mino_tx_xform_fn fn, void *user, mino_env *env);",
    :doc
    "Like mino_tx_alter_c but does NOT record a read (commute semantics).\nThe fn is invoked once eagerly to produce the call-site value; if\nthe ref did not also have an alter / ref-set in the same tx, the fn\nis replayed at commit time against the latest committed value (the\nfn must therefore be commutative). Otherwise the call-site value is\nwhat gets committed (matching JVM, which skips commute-log replay\nfor refs in the write set). Returns the call-site value, or NULL if\nthe transformer threw."}
   {:kind :function,
    :name "mino_tx_ensure",
    :return-type "mino_val *",
    :params "mino_state *S, mino_val *v, mino_env *env",
    :signature
    "mino_val *mino_tx_ensure(mino_state *S, mino_val *v, mino_env *env);",
    :doc
    "Pin the ref against any concurrent committer until this transaction\ncommits or aborts. Returns the in-tx effective value. Must be in a\ntransaction. Equivalent to (ensure ref)."}
   {:kind :typedef-fn,
    :name "mino_tx_body_fn",
    :return-type "mino_val *",
    :params "mino_state *S, void *user, mino_env *env",
    :signature
    "typedef mino_val *(*mino_tx_body_fn)(mino_state *S, void *user, mino_env *env);",
    :doc
    "C-callable transaction body, used by mino_tx_run. Returns the\nbody's last value. The body may invoke any in-tx accessor\n(mino_tx_ref_deref / mino_tx_alter_c / ...), call mino_call to\ndispatch into Clojure code, and throw via prim_throw_classified.\n\nThe body is re-invoked on commit-time conflict, up to 10000 retries\nbefore throwing eval/state MST004. Any user state mutated through\n`user` survives across retries; if clean retry semantics matter,\nsnapshot mutable state into a retry-local buffer at the top of the\nbody. mino_val * pointers captured in user state should not be\nrelied on across retries (the GC may relocate or finalize between\niterations); re-derive them from the ref / world on each call."}
   {:kind :function,
    :name "mino_tx_run",
    :return-type "mino_val *",
    :params
    "mino_state *S, mino_tx_body_fn body, void *user, mino_env *env",
    :signature
    "mino_val *mino_tx_run(mino_state *S, mino_tx_body_fn body, void *user, mino_env *env);",
    :doc
    "Run body inside a transaction. Returns body's result on commit,\nor NULL if the body threw an unhandled exception or the retry cap\nwas exhausted. Nests cleanly: if a transaction is already running\non the calling thread (started by an outer dosync or mino_tx_run),\nthe inner call is absorbed into the outer's tx and runs once\nwithout its own setjmp / retry frame. Equivalent to the host-level\n(dosync (body))."}]}
