 {:name "Record types",
  :unstable false,
  :declarations
  [{:kind :function,
    :name "mino_defrecord",
    :return-type "mino_val *",
    :params
    "mino_state *S, const char *ns, const char *name, const char *const *field_names, size_t n_fields",
    :signature
    "mino_val *mino_defrecord(mino_state *S, const char *ns, const char *name, const char *const *field_names, size_t n_fields);",
    :doc
    "Define a record type. Returns the MINO_TYPE value. The pointer is\nstable for the life of the state (record types are pinned), so type\nidentity is pointer equality.\n\nIdempotent: subsequent calls with the same ns/name return the\nexisting type so re-loading scripts is safe. Field shape on a\nre-call is ignored (the existing type wins) — the script-layer\n`defrecord` macro validates shape changes when it re-evaluates.\n\nThe strings are copied into the state's intern table on first use,\nso callers may pass stack-allocated names. Field names are\nconverted to keywords and stored in declared order.\n\nMirrors the Clojure `defrecord` macro name to make the C/script\nanalogy obvious to a C/C++/Rust embedder."}
   {:kind :function,
    :name "mino_is_record_type",
    :return-type "int",
    :params "const mino_val *v",
    :signature "int mino_is_record_type(const mino_val *v);",
    :doc "Return 1 if v is a record type (MINO_TYPE), 0 otherwise."}
   {:kind :function,
    :name "mino_record",
    :return-type "mino_val *",
    :params
    "mino_state *S, mino_val *type, mino_val **vals, size_t n_vals",
    :signature
    "mino_val *mino_record(mino_state *S, mino_val *type, mino_val **vals, size_t n_vals);",
    :doc
    "Build a record. type must be a MINO_TYPE returned by\nmino_defrecord; n_vals must equal the type's declared field count;\nvals[i] gives the value for the i-th declared field. The vals\narray is copied into a fresh malloc-owned slot vector owned by the\nreturned record. Returns NULL on type mismatch or arity mismatch\n(the caller should treat NULL as a runtime error).\n\nThe new record has no extension keys; assoc with an undeclared key\nlazily allocates the ext map."}
   {:kind :function,
    :name "mino_record_field",
    :return-type "mino_val *",
    :params "const mino_val *record, const char *name",
    :signature
    "mino_val *mino_record_field(const mino_val *record, const char *name);",
    :doc
    "Read a declared field by name. Returns the field value (borrowed)\nor NULL if name is not a declared field of record's type.\nExtension keys are not read by this entry point; embedders can\nreach them via the script-level (get r :ext-key) path."}
